Based on my research:

- **spring-aspects 6.0.0's only dependency is `aspectjweaver:1.9.9.1`** — identical to what 5.3.31 already resolves and what the CI log shows working (`aspectjweaver-1.9.9.1.jar` in the built image, analysis/build/image-creation all succeeded).
- Sibling Spring 6.0.0 modules (`spring-context`, `spring-aop`, `spring-tx`, `spring-web`, `spring-webflux`, `spring-test`) already have working native-image tests in this repo at 6.0.0, so nothing about the 6.0.0 line structurally blocks Native Image.
- The existing 5.3.31 test suite doesn't rely on runtime/load-time weaving of user code — it invokes the compile-time-woven aspects (`AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect.aspectOf()`, etc.) directly, avoiding any Native Image–incompatible weaving path.
- The log is truncated exactly where the actual nativeTest failure detail would appear (cut off after one test `SUCCESSFUL`), so there's no visible stack trace or failure signature to trace into library source. Per the rules, that alone rules out an unsupportable verdict — a red test with no visible mechanism is not evidence of a Native Image limitation, and repairable is the safe default.
- No Docker image, extra Maven dependency, or environment/system property is indicated by anything in the artifact, its POM, or its usage pattern.

